From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:14:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 53/64] gdb: do not throw from btrace_teardown when the target
 is gone

Losing the connection with btrace state left made GDB terminate while mourning.

diff --git a/gdb/btrace.c b/gdb/btrace.c
index f5f2d6da972..770b7c2eb24 100644
--- a/gdb/btrace.c
+++ b/gdb/btrace.c
@@ -2097,7 +2097,18 @@ btrace_teardown (struct thread_info *tp)
   DEBUG ("teardown thread %s (%s)", print_thread_id (tp),
 	 tp->ptid.to_string ().c_str ());
 
-  target_teardown_btrace (btp->target);
+  /* This is called when a thread goes away, e.g. while an inferior is
+     mourned after the remote connection was lost.  The target that
+     traced the thread may be gone then, and there is nothing left to
+     tear down on it; drop the thread's trace anyway.  */
+  try
+    {
+      target_teardown_btrace (btp->target);
+    }
+  catch (const gdb_exception_error &ex)
+    {
+      DEBUG ("teardown failed: %s", ex.what ());
+    }
   btp->target = NULL;
 
   btrace_clear (tp);
